menuconfig MODULES_STEP_RIG_ATT
	bool "step_rig_att"
	default n
	---help---
		Enable support for step_rig_att

		Test instrument that publishes a commanded attitude as a STEP
		and holds it, so the closed-loop step response of the attitude
		controller - rise time, peak time, overshoot, settling time -
		can be measured directly. Driven through the ATTITUDE setpoint
		path (mc_att_control) instead of raw body rates.

		The deliberate opposite of hold_rig_att. That module walks a
		leader setpoint to the target at HRATT_RATE so the controller
		never sees a large error; useful for moving a rig gently, but
		it means the observed trajectory belongs to the ramp rather
		than to the control law. Here nothing shapes the command, so
		the whole transient - saturation included - is the plant under
		test.

		The target is Eulerf(STEPATT_ROLL, STEPATT_PITCH, 0): absolute
		and zero-yaw, never composed onto a latched heading, so repeat
		runs are comparable. Thrust is fixed at STEPATT_THRUST with no
		compensation, so the vehicle descends while held at a large
		tilt - run it high, or on a fixture that cannot translate.

		Never touches position/GPS - start with `step_rig_att start`
		and do not run it alongside another OFFBOARD-publishing module.
		Requires FD_FAIL_R/FD_FAIL_P to be relaxed past 60 degrees: a
		step trips the detector mid-rise and voids the run.
